<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's April unemployment rises to 2.7 pct.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's April unemployment rises to 2.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's seasonally-adjusted unemployment rate in April rose to 2.7 percent from 1.9 percent a year earlier, provisional National Statistical Office (NSO) figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>						  April  March   April '96</p>
<p>    Unemployment (pct)		     2.7    2.9     1.9</p>
<p>						  (2.8)  (3.4)   (2.0)</p>
<p>Note: Seasonally unadjusted figures in brackets. The NSO figures showed the economically active population rose to 21.82 million in April from 21.17 million a year ago and from 21.46 million in March.</p>
</text>
